<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20651] use of non-initialised ldiskfs_block_map structure in osd_declare_write_commit.</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20651</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The osd-ldsikfs osd_declare_commit_write() function doesn't initialise ldiskfs_block_map structure before calling osd_id_mapped(), it may contains an arbitrary garbage which can be interpreted as a cached block extent.  It leads to a possible mis-calculation of tx credits and eventually may cause an ldsikfs failure.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment />
